@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@idempotencyKey = demo-subscription-001

### Check that the API and SQLite store are ready
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Browse the insurance plans and monthly prices
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/plans

### Start a simulated MTN subscription payment (XAF)
# @name createPayment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "provider": "Mtn",
  "purpose": "Subscription",
  "amount": 1000,
  "phoneNumber": "+237 6 12 34 56 78",
  "customerName": "Jean Mbarga",
  "birthDate": "1990-01-01",
  "address": "Yaoundé, Cameroun",
  "categoryId": "moto",
  "categoryName": "Accident / Moto",
  "planName": "Confort"
}

### The request above is idempotent: replaying its key returns the same payment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{
  "provider": "Mtn",
  "purpose": "Subscription",
  "amount": 1000,
  "phoneNumber": "+237 6 12 34 56 78",
  "customerName": "Jean Mbarga",
  "birthDate": "1990-01-01",
  "address": "Yaoundé, Cameroun",
  "categoryId": "moto",
  "categoryName": "Accident / Moto",
  "planName": "Confort"
}

### List payment records (find the payment id in the response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments

@paymentId = {{createPayment.response.body.$.id}}

### Simulate operator approval; a subscription is persisted atomically
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/simulator/payments/{{paymentId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "outcome": "Succeeded"
}

### Alternative test outcomes: "Failed" or "Pending"

### Query the payment state
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/{{paymentId}}

### Not found example (Problem Details 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### List contracts created by confirmed subscription payments
# @name listSubscriptions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions

@subscriptionId = {{listSubscriptions.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Inspect one contract (replace with its id from the list response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{subscriptionId}}

### Not found contract example (Problem Details 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
